      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Acute pharmacological tests were done in 47 patients with stable II-III functional class angina of effort. Indices for central hemodynamics were determined with the aid of Iu. T. Puskar' modification thoracic rheovasography techniques. In the acute test in patients with exertional angina, nitroglycerin, anaprilin, corinfar, and no-shpa tend to reduce energy expenditure on displacement of one litre of cardiac output, with corinfar being also capable of lowering total peripheral vascular resistance, no-shpa tending to augment the cardiac index and reduce total peripheral vascular resistance 30 minutes after the intake of the drug (but this effect is but of short duration: it lasts for only 30 minutes)."},
